    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0054" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg34"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 472.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 8, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my Nos. 461 and 465,
                    respecting the imprisonment of Mr. J. H. Mansfield, the United States consul at
                    Tabasco, I transmit herewith a copy of a letter of the 6th of November last,
                    addressed by Charles Jones, esq., to Mr. Adams, our minister at London, upon the
                    subject, I will thank you to ask for the release of Mr. Mansfield, that he may
                    be permitted to proceed to the United States, and you will also request
                    explanations of the proceedings against him.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
